   "text": "http : / / articles . timesofindia . indiatimes . com / 2011 - 11 - 12 / india / 30391127 _ 1 _ somali - pirate - attack - indian - warship - merchant - vessels Somali pirate <2 attack> <3 foiled> in Gulf of Aden TNN Nov 12 , 2011 , 05 . 51AM IST MUMBAI : An Indian warship on Thursday <7 intercepted> three boats with 26 Somali pirates in the Gulf of Aden and <8 foiled> an <1 attack> on merchant vessels . INS Sukanya <4 detected> five suspicious boats , speedily <5 approaching> the merchant vessels that the warship was <6 escorting> through the Internationally Recognized Transit Corridor . \"The warship immediately altered towards the suspicious vessels and challenged them . While two of them managed to escape , INS Sukanya successfully intercepted the remaining three and carried out boarding - and - search action , \" said Captain Manohar Nambiar , chief PRO ( Defence ) . The Navy confiscated 14 AK - 47 rifles , 31 magazines and 923 rounds from the boat along with grapnels , ladders and rope - handling gloves , Nambiar said . This is the fifth successful anti - piracy operation conducted by INS Sukanya , during its patrol mission in the Gulf of Aden .",
